# UI / Templates Rules

Canonical sources (read before any UI work):
1. `knowledge/design/BRAND_GUIDELINES.md` — identity
2. `knowledge/design/dx006a_design_system/` — Design System foundation (DX-006A)
3. `knowledge/design/UI_GUARDIAN.md` — enforcement / release gate (G-1…G-12)
4. Surface authorities DX-001…DX-005 as applicable
5. `knowledge/design/UI_UX_IMPLEMENTATION_STANDARD.md` — legacy UX-001; **superseded on conflict** by DX-001 / DX-006A for redesigns

UI quality is a **release blocker**. Brand defines identity; DX-006A defines tokens and components; UI Guardian governs workflow and validation. Do not invent design tokens outside the system. Pages compose components; components compose tokens.

## Mandatory workflow (before writing UI code)

1. Read Brand Guidelines + DX-006A architecture/token/catalogue/Guardian rules + UI Guardian.
2. Inspect catalogue L1–L3 and existing partials.
3. Reuse whenever possible; create new components only with COMPONENT_STANDARDS documentation.
4. Verify G-1…G-12 — then implement.

## Never invent

Colours, spacing, typography, button styles, shadows, radii, animations, icons, layouts, component behaviour, responsive rules, or accessibility behaviour. Everything originates from the design system.

## Brand colours (never invent new ones)

| Token | HEX | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Primary Blue | `#3B4FB8` | Primary actions, links, focus, charts |
| Primary Dark | `#0D1B2A` | Text / dark UI |
| Deep Navy | `#0A1628` | Elevated dark chrome |
| Midnight | `#020D24` | Dark canvases |
| Gold | `#E8B02B` | Achievement / logo / awards only |
| White | `#FFFFFF` | Surfaces / contrast |

Gold is **not** a UI colour. Never use gold for buttons, nav, links, focus, or charts. Reject random blues/greys/gradients/accents.

## Tokens (DX-006A / DX-001)

- **Spacing (product UI):** 4, 8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64 only. (12 / 96 / 128 retired for redesigns.)
- **Type:** Inter only. Display 32 (rare) / Page 24 / Section 18 / Body 16 / Supporting 14 / Caption 12.
- **Icons:** Lucide only; functional; never decorative; never replace labels without names.
- **Cards:** Only when DX-001 grouping justified; prefer border over soft shadow stacks; no KPI card grids.
- **Inputs:** Token radius, visible labels, helper/errors below, Primary focus ring; never placeholder-as-label.
- **Buttons:** Exactly **one** Primary CTA per page; Secondary / Ghost / Text / Danger as catalogue. No new variants without catalogue entry.
- **Motion:** ≤250ms ease-out; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Reject bounce/flash/shake/elastic.
- **Charts:** Semantic colours only when meaningful.

## Guardian gate (must PASS)

One Primary · One H1 · Token-only · No hard-coded colours · No duplicate spacing scales · No KPI patterns · No decorative cards · L0–L3 hierarchy · No decorative icons · No duplicate nav · Catalogue only · No Rejected components.

## Page / hierarchy gate

Answer in under five seconds: What is this page? Most important action? Where should the eye go first? What next? Prefer less content, clearer hierarchy, intentional whitespace. Avoid equal emphasis, competing CTAs, and visual noise.

## States (feature incomplete without them)

Loading · Empty (Reason + Next Action) · Success · Failure · Permission denied · Offline (where applicable). Skeleton preferred; calm microcopy (DX-003 — no blame, cheer, or stack traces).

## A11y / responsive / performance

WCAG AA (`ACCESSIBILITY_STANDARD.md`), keyboard, visible focus, ARIA, semantic HTML, large targets — failures block release. Desktop → tablet → mobile per `RESPONSIVE_STANDARD.md`: one component, responsive behaviour. Avoid layout shift, heavy animation, oversized assets, duplicate libraries.

## Jinja / CSS / JS

```
app/templates/
  layouts/     # base.html, auth_base.html
  partials/    # sidebar, topnav, flash_messages
  <feature>/
```

- Authenticated → `layouts/base.html`; auth → `layouts/auth_base.html`.
- Reuse partials / catalogue components; no screen-local design systems. Business rules stay in services.
- CSS: `app/static/css/tokens.css` is the CSS token source; feature CSS must reference tokens only.
- JS: `app/static/js/app.js` + feature files; CSRF from `<meta name="csrf-token">`; progressive enhancement; respect CSP.

## Release gate (UI Guardian)

Not complete until Brand + DX-006A + Guardian G-1…G-12 + a11y + responsive + performance pass. Self-review: Would Apple remove / Linear simplify / Notion make this easier to scan? If yes — implement the simpler solution.
